-- title:
--   Transport of component-chart reduction data along a semilinear automorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $0$ and $A\subseteq L$ a valuation subring satisfying the rank-one condition `hrk`: for every $x\neq 0$ in $L$ and every $y$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ there is $n\in\mathbb N$ with $v_A(y^n)\le v_A(x)$. Let $F$ be a field over $L$ which is a curve over $L$ (principal divisors of degree $0$, finite residue extensions, $\Omega_{F/L}$ free of rank $1$) and essentially of finite type over $L$, and let $\bar F,\bar F'$ be two fields over $\kappa=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, each a curve over $\kappa$ and essentially of finite type, all of whose places are rational (the residue field of each place is generated by $\kappa$). Let $C$ be a component chart of $F$ along $A$ with reduction $\bar F$ and $C'$ one with reduction $\bar F'$; thus each consists of a valuation subring `integers` of $F$, a surjective ring homomorphism `residue` onto the reduction with kernel the maximal ideal, a set `dom` of places of $F/L$, a finite set `nodes` of places of the reduction, and a map `placeMap` from places of $F/L$ to places of the reduction, subject to the compatibility axioms of `ComponentChart`. Assume every place in `C.dom` and in `C'.dom` is rational, and that both charts have disc fibres: for each place $Q$ of the relevant reduction which is not a node there is $T$ in the chart's `integers` whose residue is nonzero with $\mathrm{ord}_Q$ of that residue equal to $1$, such that every chart place $P$ above $Q$ has $T$ in its valuation subring with $P$-evaluation lying in the maximal ideal of $A$, and such that for every $c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ there is exactly one place $P$ of $F/L$ in the chart domain above $Q$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,T=c$. Finally let $g$ be a semilinear automorphism of $F$ over $L$ (a ring automorphism of $F$ together with one of $L$, compatible with the structure map) whose base automorphism preserves $A$ in the sense $a\in A\iff \mathrm{baseAut}(g)(a)\in A$, and assume $f\in C.\mathrm{integers}\iff g\cdot f\in C'.\mathrm{integers}$ and $P\in C.\mathrm{dom}\iff g\cdot P\in C'.\mathrm{dom}$. Then there exist a ring isomorphism $\theta:\bar F\to\bar F'$ and a bijection $\Theta$ from the places of $\bar F/\kappa$ to the places of $\bar F'/\kappa$ such that: the residue maps intertwine, $C'.\mathrm{residue}(g\cdot f)=\theta(C.\mathrm{residue}\,f)$ for all $f$ in $C.\mathrm{integers}$; orders are preserved, $\mathrm{ord}_{\Theta Q}(\theta\varphi)=\mathrm{ord}_Q(\varphi)$ for all places $Q$ of $\bar F/\kappa$ and all $\varphi\in\bar F$; $\Theta$ matches nodes with nodes in both directions; and $C'.\mathrm{placeMap}(g\cdot P)=\Theta(C.\mathrm{placeMap}\,P)$ for every $P\in C.\mathrm{dom}$. Note that $\theta$ is asserted only as a ring isomorphism, and $\Theta$ only as a bijection of place sets compatible with $\theta$ through the order functions.
--
--   This is the two-chart, equivariant form of the rigidity of semistable reduction data: an automorphism of $F$ which is semilinear over an automorphism of $L$ stabilising $A$ and which matches the Gauss rings and chart domains of two disc-fibred component charts induces an isomorphism of the two reductions together with a compatible bijection of their places, nodes and reduction maps. It feeds the construction of the Galois action on the reduction of a semistable model, used in the study of the rational points and annuli attached at the nodes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_ComponentChart_exists_equiv_placeMap_smul_eq_of_forall_mem_integers_iff_of_forall_mem_dom_iff_of_discFibres.lean

